{
  "title": "Traffic Management for Works on Roads Code of Practice",
  "abstract": "The Traffic Management for Works on Roads Code of Practice is the primary reference document for all traffic management activities on Western Australian roads. Published by Main Roads Western Australia (MRWA), this code establishes the mandatory requirements and standards that must be followed when conducting any work on roads.\n\nThe code adopts and adapts the Austroads Guide to Temporary Traffic Management (AGTTM) for Western Australian conditions. It covers the roles and responsibilities of all parties involved in traffic management, from Traffic Management Supervisors to Traffic Controllers, and establishes the requirements for traffic management plans, variations, and notifications.\n\nKey topics include traffic guidance scheme requirements, signage standards, speed zoning, pedestrian management, mobile works, short-term low-impact works, and emergency setups. All Traffic Controllers must be familiar with this code as it forms the basis of competency requirements and legal compliance for traffic management work in WA. The May 2025 edition is the current version and supersedes all previous editions.",
  "keywords": ["code-of-practice", "traffic-management", "standards"],
